From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] music: seek an MP3 before locking the audio

Mix_FadeInMusicPos() seeked with the audio locked. The first seek into an
MP3 builds dr_mp3's seek table (70-80 ms for a few minutes of music on
the ODROID-GO Advance), and meanwhile the audio callback waited: with a
buffer of 46 ms the sound broke up when VCMI resumed a track (the end of
a battle, of a turn).

A music that is not playing is seeked before the audio is locked; the
seek under the lock is then quick, as the table is there.

Upstream: not submitted
Signed-off-by: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
---
 src/music.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/music.c b/src/music.c
index 5b4030b..da1692e 100644
--- a/src/music.c
+++ b/src/music.c
@@ -889,6 +889,16 @@ int Mix_FadeInMusicPos(Mix_Music *music, int loops, int ms, double position)
     music->fade_step = 0;
     music->fade_steps = (ms + ms_per_step - 1) / ms_per_step;
 
+    /*
+     * The audio callback waits while the audio is locked, and a seek can
+     * take long: dr_mp3 builds its seek table on the first one. A music that
+     * is not playing is seeked before; the seek under the lock is then quick.
+     */
+    if (position > 0.0 && music != music_playing &&
+        music->interface->api == MIX_MUSIC_DRMP3 && music->interface->Seek) {
+        music->interface->Seek(music->context, position);
+    }
+
     /* Play the puppy */
     Mix_LockAudio();
     /* If the current music is fading out, wait for the fade to complete */
